 3. Snap IRL 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Rebecca Zisser/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Social media might make you feel isolated , but Snapchat thinks it has a solution for that.

 The app today rolled out Snapchat Plans , a feature that allows users to schedule and coordinate plans with their friends to meet up in real life. Zoom in: People can use the feature to invite up to 200 friends to an event or meetup, receive invitations and get reminders.

 The feature is private. 💭 Nathan's thought bubble: Social apps are beginning to recognize that America's epidemic of loneliness translates into a hunger for IRL experiences.

 
 
